1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,952
And so this curve
now is something

2
00:00:01,952 --> 00:00:05,455
that we understand and we
understand how to control it.

3
00:00:05,455 --> 00:00:13,163
And if you go back to the
example of making glass tough,

4
00:00:13,163 --> 00:00:17,534
I was just showing you these
ions, these sodium ions.

5
00:00:17,534 --> 00:00:19,069
They're left in there.

6
00:00:19,069 --> 00:00:23,807
Well, it turns out that you
can put ions into glass,

7
00:00:23,807 --> 00:00:26,810
and maybe you're doing it
to change the viscosity

8
00:00:26,810 --> 00:00:29,513
so the thing stays
liquid for longer,

9
00:00:29,513 --> 00:00:33,250
and you can maybe work with
it in different regimes.

10
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:35,018
But maybe you're putting
the ions in there

11
00:00:35,018 --> 00:00:38,288
to do something else.

12
00:00:38,288 --> 00:00:41,858
And so actually there's
a whole another thing

13
00:00:41,858 --> 00:00:46,530
you can do once you have ions
in the glass like sodium.

14
00:00:46,530 --> 00:00:49,499
You can substitute them out.

15
00:00:49,499 --> 00:00:52,135
Imagine that I
have-- that's what

16
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,503
this next picture is showing.

17
00:00:53,503 --> 00:00:57,174
Imagine that I've
got a glass in here,

18
00:00:57,174 --> 00:01:00,510
and those red
circles are sodium.

19
00:01:00,510 --> 00:01:03,780
But now I've introduced a
different ion on the surface.

20
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:05,782
That's potassium.

21
00:01:05,782 --> 00:01:06,516
What happens?

22
00:01:06,516 --> 00:01:09,786
Well, if I have a high
concentration of potassium

23
00:01:09,786 --> 00:01:11,621
and I put it on a
surface of glass that

24
00:01:11,621 --> 00:01:14,257
has a bunch of
sodium in it, so now

25
00:01:14,257 --> 00:01:18,929
I've got a glass with
sodium ions in it.

26
00:01:18,929 --> 00:01:24,835
And I expose it to
a potassium bath.

27
00:01:24,835 --> 00:01:29,005
So now I've got
potassium up here.

28
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:32,442
And what happens is if the
concentration is high enough

29
00:01:32,442 --> 00:01:34,711
and the conditions are
right, I can get potassium

30
00:01:34,711 --> 00:01:38,215
to go in for the sodium.

31
00:01:38,215 --> 00:01:41,284
And so actually now
I can substitute.

32
00:01:41,284 --> 00:01:43,453
So these were here.

33
00:01:43,453 --> 00:01:46,957
I can now substitute
those for potassium.
